        "current_synthesis": "Observed: T1 learned from zero to high complete-hold success, reaching 0.97 at checkpoint-100352 by 100352 steps, then fluctuating or regressing through 120832 steps. This establishes learnability of the current state-based PPO recipe on the outer-radius training distribution, not attainment of the human goal. Competing explanations remain: (1) the principal gap is distributional, because the policy never trains on official inner-radius targets where folded configurations and different Jacobians apply; (2) the principal gap is transient control, where reach or deceleration leaves residual velocity and interrupts the 100-step hold even on familiar geometry. The training dynamics alone cannot distinguish these explanations, and no claim about official success or branch preference is justified.",
